+### Base-layer restoration
+
+The `$reverted` map names selectors and longhands to roll back inside preflight's own `base` layer.
+It applies to an attribute-sized replaced element whose box a `base`-layer preflight rule changes.
+The `revert` mixin, called by the `restore` mixin, emits one rule per entry after preflight under the recipe.
+Both Bootstrap partials default the map to empty; only the Tailwind token partial configures it.
+The object-fit entry selects `:is(img, video):is(.NAME, ...)` across
+`object-fit-{,sm-,md-,lg-,xl-,xxl-}{contain,cover,fill,none,scale}` and writes
+`display: revert-layer; max-width: revert-layer; height: revert-layer`.
+The selector wins over preflight by specificity and rolls those properties back to the preceding layers and the element's attributes.
+A reversion from the `bootstrap` layer cannot remove declarations in `base`.
+
+The `restores attribute-sized boxes for all object-fit names and leaves a bare image on preflight`
+case reads a 64×64 border box for every one of the 30 names on a 160×80 SVG with
+`width="64" height="64"`, with computed fits `contain`, `cover`, `fill`, `none`, and `scale-down`.
+Its bare control reads 64×32, `display: block`, and `max-width: 100%`.
+The `places the object-fit restoration in base with exactly its names and longhands` case pins the rule's selector, layer, and declarations;
+see the [Tailwind face proofs](../tests/src/tailwindcss/index.test.ts).
+The ordinary `$restored` map retains its 11 `revert` rules; `$reverted` adds one rule with 3 declarations.
